What:		/proc/game_opt/cpu_min_freq
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write ColorOS 14 GameOpt minimum CPU-frequency request derived
		from the OnePlus 9R Android 14 interface.  A write contains one or
		more whitespace-separated CPU:kHz pairs, for example:

		0:960000 4:1440000 7:1785600

		A request applies to the entire cpufreq policy shared by the named
		CPU.  Multiple pairs for one policy use the lowest-numbered named
		CPU, matching the donor's policy traversal.  The complete write is
		validated before any request changes.  Duplicate CPUs, malformed
		pairs, absent CPUs, empty writes, and writes of 256 bytes or more are
		rejected.  Reading reports the stored request for each present CPU.
		The boot default is 0, which imposes no minimum limit.
Users:		vendor.oplus.hardware.gameopt-service

What:		/proc/game_opt/cpu_max_freq
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write ColorOS 14 GameOpt maximum CPU-frequency request.  Input,
		policy sharing, validation, and output use the same rules as
		cpu_min_freq.  The boot default is UINT_MAX, which imposes no maximum
		limit.  Both controls use the kernel's existing CPUFREQ_ADJUST policy
		notifier and add no scheduler hot-path hook.
Users:		vendor.oplus.hardware.gameopt-service
